77-670b-5f03-a0b5-e6f76acf7677" :question/math-academy-id "q-7696" :question/problem "Express ${\\cos }^{2}⁡{41}^{∘}-{\\sin }^{2}⁡{41}^{∘}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{\\cos }^{2}⁡x-{\\sin }^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={41}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\cos }^{2}⁡{41}^{∘}-{\\sin }^{2}⁡{41}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {41}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡{82}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698875 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08535e2c-8ed8-5b0d-ad03-0cd1d354b13e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos 46^\\circ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698874} {:answer/id #uuid "299f81d6-60f5-51c0-9430-e498b718ec5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\cos 46^\\circ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698878} {:answer/id #uuid "854ab903-dcae-5051-af7f-0ef5a3c22338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos 23^\\circ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698885} {:answer/id #uuid "bb2c596e-1431-5639-914e-71af83efb0e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin 46^\\circ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698888} {:answer/id #uuid "db4d2f4b-c98b-58e1-90ef-51dd2e9e2342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos 46^\\circ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db4d2f4b-c98b-58e1-90ef-51dd2e9e2342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos 46^\\circ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698889} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c2ef057-524e-5cd8-90b8-6bc82cc5964f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698876}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b60734f-6cd6-58cc-88a5-3253cd601645" :question/problem "Express\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 23^\\circ-\\sin^2 23^\\circ\n$$\n\nas a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "Recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x-\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x).\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=23^\\circ$ and double the angle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos^2 23^\\circ-\\sin^2 23^\\circ\n&=\\cos(2\\cdot23^\\circ) \\\\\n&=\\cos 46^\\circ.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe angle doubles; there is no extra coefficient outside the cosine."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698882 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "008bdba5-b60f-52d0-8744-47acf0faa945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos^2 38^\\circ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698873} {:answer/id #uuid "3147e14a-005d-5d87-889e-f865df461eab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos 19^\\circ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698879} {:answer/id #uuid "759b5816-4b6c-5de2-b111-b03de2af74c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos 38^\\circ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698884} {:answer/id #uuid "9fa4cbe4-69b5-5510-a48e-01d660ee8652" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos 76^\\circ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698887} {:answer/id #uuid "f00c0934-bb1b-5af7-8f58-d3ca227966c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos 38^\\circ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f00c0934-bb1b-5af7-8f58-d3ca227966c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos 38^\\circ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698892} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc7e8539-e0ee-52fe-ab20-d1109820fe13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698890}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6876b3d3-10b5-5357-a52d-52e5ecb514f0" :question/problem "Express\n\n$$\n2\\cos^4 19^\\circ-2\\sin^4 19^\\circ\n$$\n\nas a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "Factor out $2$, then use the difference of squares $a^2-b^2=(a-b)(a+b)$ with $a=\\cos^2 19^\\circ$ and $b=\\sin^2 19^\\circ$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&2\\cos^4 19^\\circ-2\\sin^4 19^\\circ \\\\\n&\\quad=2\\left(\\cos^4 19^\\circ-\\sin^4 19^\\circ\\right) \\\\\n&\\quad=2\\left(\\cos^2 19^\\circ-\\sin^2 19^\\circ\\right)\n\\left(\\cos^2 19^\\circ+\\sin^2 19^\\circ\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe Pythagorean identity gives $\\cos^2 19^\\circ+\\sin^2 19^\\circ=1$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n2\\cos^4 19^\\circ-2\\sin^4 19^\\circ\n=2\\left(\\cos^2 19^\\circ-\\sin^2 19^\\circ\\right).\n$$\n\nNow apply $\\cos^2 x-\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)$ with $x=19^\\circ$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\left(\\cos^2 19^\\circ-\\sin^2 19^\\circ\\right)\n&=2\\cos(2\\cdot19^\\circ) \\\\\n&=2\\cos 38^\\circ.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe fourth powers form a difference of squares, not the square of a difference. Factor before using the double-angle formula."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698883 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "294bd9f5-ba5d-5a7b-a121-7a217e4d5b0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{7}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698877} {:answer/id #uuid "598020cf-28d7-59dc-a5b6-85c5447e5db0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{7}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698881} {:answer/id #uuid "933f4095-d094-583b-97c5-6b38272a40fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{28}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698886} {:answer/id #uuid "ee2c1ec0-5a82-55ec-9684-5827f0a13dd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{14}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698891} {:answer/id #uuid "fe93bbec-c6b6-5858-b29f-55e18fb5af92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{7}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "294bd9f5-ba5d-5a7b-a121-7a217e4d5b0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{7}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698877} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a475d62-27ce-5e13-9061-83c148ab0fc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698880}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6a99ee1a-6952-50c8-b2e2-c34bd2679a28" :question/problem "Express\n\n$$\n2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{14}\\right)-2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{14}\\right)\n$$\n\nas a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First factor out the common coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{14}\\right)-2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{14}\\right) \\\\\n&\\quad=2\\left(\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{14}\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{14}\\right)\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall $\\cos^2 x-\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)$. With $x=\\frac{\\pi}{14}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\left(\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{14}\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{14}\\right)\\right)\n&=2\\cos\\left(2\\cdot\\frac{\\pi}{14}\\right) \\\\\n&=2\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{7}\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the common factor $2$ outside the cosine; only the angle inside doubles."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698945 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1eeb43e7-6285-5dc7-bbaa-8eed178c5ecc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\cos\\left(10^\\circ\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698943} {:answer/id #uuid "22c5cf4f-a743-54e0-a9c6-3598535c1e19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\cos\\left(5^\\circ\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698944} {:answer/id #uuid "4149d65a-382d-53be-9c3b-5f3d0597de7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos\\left(20^\\circ\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698951} {:answer/id #uuid "72e4d719-1361-5a99-a89f-03bd5f8b16c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos\